  "title": "The Wet Floor Warning Needs a Route",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "public safety/preparedness",
  "premise": "A facility team wants people to notice a temporary walking hazard, but a lone sign appears too late in the fictional approach. A reviewed plan considers visibility and an accessible alternative without asking viewers to step through the hazard.",
  "hook": "Can the warning be seen before the choice is made?",
  "visible_action": "A walking path approaches a symbolic wet area; sightlines reveal the late sign and a reviewed route overlay pauses for approval.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A warning should be evaluated from the user’s actual approach and available choices.",
  "gate": "Require local facilities and accessibility review; no claim that a sign alone controls a hazard. Do not ask viewers to guess an emergency response or choose an action in a simulated emergency; any response content must come from reviewed official guidance.",
